# Resource: signalfx_observability_directory

Terraform owns the complete ordered Template membership list for the Directory. Give `templates` Template IDs; their order controls their order in the UI. A membership update replaces the backend's entire list; it is not an atomic add or remove operation. The Directory API provides no ETag or other stale-write precondition, so concurrent UI, API, or Terraform changes are last-write-wins and can be lost.

Use a writable path under your own `~users/<email>/...` namespace, or under `~organization/<group>/...` with the required group permissions. Other roots may be read-only. The default is an empty membership list and `pinned = true`, so a path with no Templates remains occupied. An unpinned Directory must have at least one Template membership.

After manually importing an existing Directory, add every membership that Terraform should retain to `templates` before applying; otherwise, the next apply removes them. Generated import configuration includes the memberships observed during import. Creation refuses occupied paths; import them to manage an existing entry. The API does not distinguish an unoccupied path from a stored empty, unpinned entry.

Destroying the Directory removes its membership links but does not delete the referenced Template records. Deletion is refused when the path has child directories or is an identity, canonical, or reserved service-managed entry.

